#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:5 cca62a2c0d6c48518774f92a83d1b6e0
msgid "Common Issues and Fixes"
msgstr "常见问题与解决方法"

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:7 6bfe5abbbded4b5da26576e633e61e10
msgid ""
"This page details some of the most common issues with Balance Bots and "
"possible solutions."
msgstr "本页详细介绍了平衡机器人最常见的问题及可能的解决方案。"

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:10
#: 5a4195236d01414894a0fd259a7cc493
msgid "1) Manual/Hold Mode issues:"
msgstr "1) Manual/Hold 模式问题："

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:13
#: 4a74f9efd9684eaea9eb69928627cbe6
msgid "The vehicle struggles to balance or wobbles too much"
msgstr "车辆难以保持平衡或抖动过大"

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:15
#: 0aa42e78b05b42c58d4ac6a484dad144
msgid ""
"**1) Motor Backlash** : The balancing depends on very fine adjustments of "
"the wheel. So any backlash between gears of the motor could lead to poor "
"balancing performance."
msgstr "**1) 电机齿轮间隙**：平衡控制依赖于对车轮的精细调节，因此电机齿轮之间的任何间隙都会导致平衡性能下降。"

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:18
#: b76e067b36af4c7eadf9c88f81d8de60
msgid "This is bad:"
msgstr "以下情况较差："

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:23
#: d4c4c55bdd084fedbb48efab36eab442
msgid ""
"The only fix is to change motors. Make sure the backlash is as low as "
"possible."
msgstr "唯一的解决方法是更换电机。确保齿轮间隙尽可能小。"

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:25
#: 05b942bc05db4749a9e555a75e8230d2
msgid ""
"**2) Weight Distribution** : If the center of gravity is near the wheels, "
"the vehicle can topple quickly and if the motors are not fast enough to "
"compensate, then the vehicle can become wobbly. The higher the center of "
"gravity, the slower the vehicle falls. But more torque would be required "
"from the motors to keep it balanced."
msgstr ""
"**2) "
"重心分布**：若重心靠近车轮，车辆会迅速倾倒，若电机响应不够快无法补偿，车辆就会晃动。重心越高，车辆倾倒越慢，但电机需要提供更大扭矩来维持平衡。"

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:28
#: 14f5a3de5e0143238086edd94c11ff48
msgid ""
"A good way to change the weight distribution is to move up/down the position"
" of the batteries. How high depends on the torque and speed of the motors. "
"In case of very fast motors with low torque, keep it closer to the wheels. "
"If instead the motors are slow, but can provide high torque, then shift the "
"center of mass higher by placing the batteries higher."
msgstr ""
"调整重心分布的好方法是上下移动电池位置。具体高度取决于电机的扭矩和转速。若电机转速很快但扭矩较小，应将电池放置在靠近车轮的位置；若电机转速较慢但扭矩较大，则应将电池放置得更高，以提升重心。"

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:31
#: 031d4687e7064477af7e0d4386d45e46
msgid ""
"**3) Minimum Throttle** : If the minimum throttle sent to the motors from "
"the autopilot is **too low** to turn on the motors, then the Balance Bot "
"will move back and forth struggling to keep balance. Sometimes this issue "
"can also cause it to drift off in one direction and topple. If the minimum "
"throttle value is **too high** then the Balance Bot will be able maintain "
"balance, but will be very wobbly. Refer to this guide to set the "
":ref:`minimum throttle <balance_bot-configure-throttle>` value correctly."
msgstr ""
"**3) "
"最小油门**：若自动驾驶仪发送给电机的最小油门**过低**以至于无法启动电机，平衡机器人将来回移动以试图保持平衡。有时这个问题还会导致车辆向一侧漂移并倾倒。若最小油门值**过高**，平衡机器人虽能保持平衡，但会非常晃动。请参阅本指南正确设置"
" :ref:`最小油门 <balance_bot-configure-throttle>` 值。"

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:34
#: bb46eb596adf45749fd506e8db6e09bb
msgid ""
"**4) PID tuning** : Improper PID tuning, especially high P or I gains can "
"cause the vehicle to become wobbly. An insufficient D gain can also make the"
" vehicle wobbly, but a very high D gain can cause very fast wobbling."
msgstr ""
"**4) PID 调参**：PID 调参不当，尤其是 P 或 I 增益过高会导致车辆晃动。D 增益不足也会导致车辆晃动，但 D "
"增益过高则会导致非常快速的抖动。"

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:39
#: 8d28b95d1e9a4cdc9335bed1a10f1f86
msgid "The vehicle drifts off in one direction"
msgstr "车辆向一侧漂移"

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:41
#: 9ba625b03e2a427dbab23875a8b333e8
msgid ""
"**1) Accelerometer Calibration** : This can happen because the accelerometer"
" calibration is invalid. Disturbing the autopilot, changing connections, "
"crashes etc can disturb the acceleromter calibration. Do the accelerometer "
"calibration again. Often, a one axis acccelerometer trim can fix this."
msgstr ""
"**1) "
"加速度计校准**：这可能是由于加速度计校准失效引起的。碰撞自动驾驶仪、更改连接、发生碰撞等情况都可能破坏加速度计校准。请重新进行加速度计校准，通常单轴加速度计微调即可解决此问题。"

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:44
#: aefb5f88b995407cb2d8a8eacd54d030
msgid ""
"**2) Pitch trim** : The center of mass of the vehicle be slightly displaced "
"from the zero pitch position. Hence the vehicle is not in equilibrium at 0 "
"degrees pitch. This can be offset by :ref:`setting the pitch trim "
"<balance_bot-tuning-pitch-trim>` parameter."
msgstr ""
"**2) 俯仰微调**：车辆的重心可能略微偏离零俯仰角位置，导致车辆在 0 度俯仰角时无法保持平衡。可通过 :ref:`设置俯仰微调 "
"<balance_bot-tuning-pitch-trim>` 参数来补偿。"

